WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:00.858
Troubleshooting llama.

00:00:00.858 --> 00:00:02.754
cpp starts by separating symptoms.

00:00:02.754 --> 00:00:07.684
Slow model loading may point to disk speed, file size, or storage location.

00:00:07.684 --> 00:00:12.235
Slow prompt processing may come from excessive context length or CPU-bound work.

00:00:12.235 --> 00:00:17.164
Slow token generation may come from model size, quantization choice, missing GPU acceleration,

00:00:17.164 --> 00:00:19.060
thermal throttling, or hardware limits.

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:23.232
Out-of-memory errors point toward model size, context length, or offload settings.

00:00:23.232 --> 00:00:27.024
GPU offload is helpful only when the runtime, drivers, hardware,

00:00:27.024 --> 00:00:28.920
and model configuration support it.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:34.608
Too little VRAM may limit how much of the model can run on the GPU.

00:00:34.608 --> 00:00:37.641
Too aggressive offload can fail or become unstable.

00:00:37.641 --> 00:00:42.192
CPU inference may still be useful for smaller models or low-volume workflows,

00:00:42.192 --> 00:00:45.605
but it should be recognized as a performance tradeoff.

00:00:45.605 --> 00:00:49.776
Quantization tradeoffs can look like quality problems, speed problems, or both.

00:00:49.776 --> 00:00:53.947
A very small quantization may fit easily but produce weaker answers.

00:00:53.947 --> 00:00:58.877
A larger variant may answer better but run too slowly or exceed memory.

00:00:58.877 --> 00:01:01.152
Context length can also distort results:

00:01:01.152 --> 00:01:06.461
large context may help document workflows but increase memory pressure and prompt processing time.

00:01:06.461 --> 00:01:08.736
Measure before changing too many settings.

00:01:08.736 --> 00:01:13.666
Keep a baseline prompt, record model file, context length, offload setting, sampling settings,

00:01:13.666 --> 00:01:14.804
and observed speed.

00:01:14.804 --> 00:01:17.079
Change one variable at a time.

00:01:17.079 --> 00:01:20.492
Distinguish model quality problems from runtime, prompt formatting, hardware,

00:01:20.492 --> 00:01:21.630
and configuration problems.

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:26.180
A disciplined troubleshooting loop saves time and creates knowledge you can reuse.
